WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.534
In this video, you'll learn about Sponsored Brands, a solution that helps you build your brand on

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:09.440
Amazon to better reach shoppers as they consider which products to purchase.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:15.350
We'll explore how Sponsored Brands work and how it can help you meet your campaign objectives by

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.980
connecting you directly with shoppers looking for products similar to yours.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:24.506
As a note, Sponsored Brands are available for professional sellers or vendors who have enrolled

00:00:24.506 --> 00:00:25.980
in Amazon Brand Registry.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:32.127
Sponsored Brands ads appear in placements above, alongside, and below shopping results, as well

00:00:32.127 --> 00:00:34.180
as within product detail pages.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.128
Sponsored Brands campaigns are designed to help increase awareness and consideration around your

00:00:39.128 --> 00:00:44.260
brand, but also to inspire shoppers to visit your page and finally make a purchase.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:50.100
Sponsored Brands ads include your brand's logo and headline alongside a collection of your products.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:54.000
You have control over your ad's messaging and creatives.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:59.377
Similar to Sponsored Products, Sponsored Brands use a cost-per-click model, meaning you only pay

00:00:59.377 --> 00:01:00.920
when shoppers click your ads.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:07.110
This lets you choose how much you want to bid per click and control how much you spend on campaigns

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:07.400
overall.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.525
Now that you know how Sponsored Brands can help you engage shoppers, let's learn how to get started

00:01:12.525 --> 00:01:13.580
with your first campaign.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.160
Number one, define your campaign goal.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.020
It's important to know what business goal you want to accomplish with advertising.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:26.031
Remember, Sponsored Brands campaigns can be great at helping shoppers to discover and consider your

00:01:26.031 --> 00:01:26.400
brand.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:32.523
You may want to focus on metrics like product detail page views, impressions, or new to brand metrics

00:01:32.523 --> 00:01:35.680
to see if your ads are helping reach new shoppers.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.740
Number two, create a campaign.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:41.780
Now that your goals are ready, sign in to your advertising console account.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:46.240
Click the Create Campaign button and choose Sponsored Brands.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.864
Number three, choose your campaign settings, choose a campaign name that's easy to identify and

00:01:51.864 --> 00:01:52.180
remember.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:55.280
Note that this campaign name is only visible to you.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.120
Follow this by entering the start and end dates for your campaign.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:04.915
Remember, it's recommended to create your campaign with no end date so it can run year round unless

00:02:04.915 --> 00:02:06.720
you have a specific seasonal goal.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.500
Finally, set your budget.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:14.240
You have the flexibility to choose between a daily budget or lifetime budget during campaign creation.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:19.260
Your budget should be high enough to keep your ads showing throughout your selected campaign duration.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.860
Number four, select an ad format.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.360
Sponsored Brands gives you access to three ad formats.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.100
Ad formats are templates that help you create ads based on what you'd like to promote.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.338
Product collection ad format lets you promote your products and offers the opportunity to create

00:02:35.338 --> 00:02:38.900
a more rich shopping experience through the use of branded imagery.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:44.807
Store Spotlight ad format lets you take advantage of your store, helping shoppers more easily discover

00:02:44.807 --> 00:02:47.520
the different product categories available within your store.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:54.720
Video ad format displays six to 45 seconds, auto-playing video in mobile and desktop shopping results.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.860
Number five, choose your products.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:01.762
Select the products that you want to advertise from the list of eligible products displayed from

00:03:01.762 --> 00:03:02.320
your catalog.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:06.160
You must feature at least three products but no more than 100.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.540
Choose products in the same category or products with similar keywords.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:14.993
Note that the campaign will automatically pause for sponsored brands if linking to a product list

00:03:14.993 --> 00:03:17.500
page with less than two in-stock products.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.000
Number six, set up your ad creative.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.840
Now you can customize your ad.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.200
Choose your brand name and create a headline to help tell a story about your brand.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:31.000
You can also add custom images of your brand or products to further enhance your story.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:36.000
Finally, choose the order in which you'd like your products to appear when shoppers click your ad.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.620
Number seven, choose your targeting tactic.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:43.280
Sponsored brands gives you the option to choose between keyword and product targeting.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:47.740
Keyword targeting lets you choose keywords to help your product appear in shopping results.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.720
Product targeting lets you choose categories or specific products to target your ad to.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:58.220
You can also further refine product targeting by brand, price range, or review ratings.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.680
Number eight, add negative targeting.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:05.678
Depending on which targeting tactic you choose, you will have an option to add negative targeting

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.540
to your campaign.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:11.632
Negative targeting prevents your ads from appearing on specific shopping results or detail pages

00:04:11.632 --> 00:04:13.660
that don't meet your performance goals.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.840
This in turn can refine your audience and improve your return on ad spend.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:19.860
Number nine, define your bidding.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.887
You have the flexibility to choose your cost per click bid during campaign creation and can change

00:04:24.887 --> 00:04:25.980
it at any time.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.940
Choose your bid based on the maximum amount you're willing to pay when a shopper clicks your ad.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:35.800
Once you complete these steps, you are ready to launch your first sponsored brands campaign.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:41.500
Sponsored brands' ads require approval and must be submitted for review prior to publishing.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:46.440
It's important to consider how sponsored brands fits into your broader advertising strategy.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:51.651
You can use sponsored brands to drive broader awareness and consideration for your brand and use

00:04:51.651 --> 00:04:52.303
sponsored products

00:04:52.303 --> 00:04:55.560
to reach high-intent shoppers looking to make a purchase.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:56.860
Ready to get started?

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.370
Visit ads.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:04:58.965
amazon.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:04:59.560
com
